+**Updates from GitHub Releases.** When `main` has a version with no GitHub Release yet,
+`.github/workflows/release.yml` builds the macOS app (zip and `.dmg`) and the Windows installer and
+publishes them as Release `vX.Y.Z`. Those builds carry the `github` update channel
+(`GDW_UPDATE_CHANNEL=github` when `scripts/version.py build-info` runs). Every 6 hours
+(`github_check_interval_s`) they ask GitHub for the latest release, download this platform's asset
+(`GameDevWorkstation-X.Y.Z-macos-arm64.zip` or `GameDevWorkstation-X.Y.Z-x64-setup.exe`) into the
+updates folder and write `release.json` and `latest.json` there. From then on the folder updater
+above takes over. Local builds never call GitHub. Set the repository with `[updates] github_repo`.
+
+**Automatic install.** With `[updates] auto_install = true` (the default), the app installs a
+pending update by itself once no session is running. It tries each version once, so a failed
+install never loops; install it from the banner instead, and check the update log.
+
+**Windows.** A release is an NSIS installer. A PowerShell helper, detached from the app, closes the
+app (and stops it after 30 s), waits for the backend to exit, runs the installer silently (`/S`) and
+starts the app again. If the installer fails, it starts the version that is still installed. The
+log is `update.log` in the app's logs folder. Rollback is macOS-only.
+
 **Roll back to previous** (same page) swaps in the kept version the same way. Rolling back
 again goes forward. Install only works in the built app; when you run from source, the page
 says so.
